Q: Python algorithm to automatically propagate inequalities transitively A: <p>You just need to add a few lines to your <strong>add_inequality()</strong> method. These lines go through the <strong>inequalities</strong> and check if the new inequality implies, with any of the existing ones, the need for a new one, and consequently add it.</p>
<pre><code>def add_inequality(self, m, n):
    &quot;&quot;&quot;
        Add an inequality to the registry.
         - m: the name of the first line segment
         - n: the name of the second line segment
    &quot;&quot;&quot;
    # a &lt; b   b &lt; c
    for ineq in self.inequalities:
        if ineq == (m, n):
            assert False, f&quot;Inequality {m} &lt; {n} already exists in the registry.&quot;
        if ineq == (n, m):
            assert False, f&quot;Inequality {n} &lt; {m} already exists in the registry.&quot;

    self.inequalities.append( (m, n) )

    ineqB = ( m, n )
    for ineqA in self.inequalities:
        if ineqA[ 1 ] == ineqB[ 0 ] and ineqA[ 0 ] != ineqB[ 1 ] and ( ineqA[ 0 ], neqB[ 1 ] ) not in self.inequalities:
            self.inequalities.append( ( ineqA[ 0 ], ineqB[ 1 ] ) )
</code></pre>

Q: WPF strange freezing, related to ICommand.CanExecuteChanged? A: <p>This doesn't answer the root of the question—the reason for GUI freezes. But it does offer advice on how best to implement commands without a delegate. Event execution itself doesn't depend on the presence of the CanExecute delegate. Potentially, there might be a slight speedup in checking the command state. But such a speedup would be minimal. I think it would be very difficult to detect, even in dedicated tests.</p>
<p>But leaving aside the necessity of such a thing, I'll expand on your idea of ​​disabling the subscription and checking the command state.
If there's no delegate, there's no point in checking for its presence every time.
It's better to implement two classes and a factory for creating an instance.</p>
<p>Example (not complete—basically pseudo-code).</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>    /// &lt;summary&gt;Simplified implementation of &lt;see cref=&quot;ICommand&quot;/&gt;.&lt;/summary&gt;
    public class RelayCommand : ICommand
    {
        // Simple event declaration via delegate.
        public event EventHandler? CanExecuteChanged;

        // In the base implementation without a delegate, CanExecute always returns true.
        public virtual bool CanExecute(object? parameter) =&gt; true;

        private readonly Action&lt;object?&gt; _execute;
        public void Execute(object? parameter) =&gt; _execute(parameter);

        // In the Base implementation, the constructor only accepts the Execute delegate.
        protected RelayCommand(Action&lt;object?&gt; execute)
        {
            _execute = execute ?? throw new ArgumentNullException(nameof(execute));
        }

        /// &lt;summary&gt;A method that raises &lt;see cref=&quot;CanExecuteChanged&quot;/&gt; event,
        /// which is listened for by consumers of this instance.&lt;/summary&gt;
        public void RaiseCanExecuteChanged() =&gt; CanExecuteChanged?.Invoke(this, EventArgs.Empty);

        // A private command class that accepts a CanExecute delegate.
        private class RelayCommandExecute : RelayCommand
        {
            // A delegate holding a method subscribed to CommandManager.RequerySuggested.
            // This is necessary because the subscription to CommandManager.RequerySuggested is weak.
            private readonly EventHandler _requerySuggested;

            // Overloading the RaiseCanExecuteChanged() method to avoid unnecessary nested method calls
            // when the CommandManager.RequerySuggested event occurs/
            private void RaiseCanExecuteChanged(object? sender, EventArgs e)
                =&gt; CanExecuteChanged?.Invoke(this, EventArgs.Empty);

            private readonly Predicate&lt;object?&gt; _canExecute;

            public override bool CanExecute(object? parameter) =&gt; _canExecute(parameter);

            public RelayCommandExecute(Action&lt;object?&gt; execute, Predicate&lt;object?&gt; canExecute)
                : base(execute)
            {
                _canExecute = canExecute ?? throw new ArgumentNullException(nameof(canExecute));

                // Initializing the delegate and
                // it subscribing to the CommandManager.RequerySuggested event/
                _requerySuggested = RaiseCanExecuteChanged;
                CommandManager.RequerySuggested += _requerySuggested;
            }

        }

        // Two static factory methods for receiving commands.

        /// &lt;summary&gt;Returns a command only for &lt;see cref=&quot;ICommand.Execute(object?)&quot;/&gt; method.
        /// &lt;see cref=&quot;ICommand.CanExecute(object?)&quot;/&gt; method always returns &lt;see langword=&quot;true&quot;/&gt;.&lt;/summary&gt;
        /// &lt;param name=&quot;execute&quot;&gt;Method for &lt;see cref=&quot;ICommand.Execute(object?)&quot;/&gt;.&lt;/param&gt;
        /// &lt;returns&gt;&lt;see cref=&quot;RelayCommand&quot;/&gt;.&lt;/returns&gt;
        /// &lt;exception cref=&quot;ArgumentNullException&quot;&gt;&lt;paramref name=&quot;execute&quot;/&gt; is &lt;see langword=&quot;null&quot;/&gt;.&lt;/exception&gt;
        public static RelayCommand Create(Action&lt;object?&gt; execute)
            =&gt; new RelayCommand(execute);

        /// &lt;summary&gt;Returns a command for &lt;see cref=&quot;ICommand.Execute(object?)&quot;/&gt; and
        /// &lt;see cref=&quot;ICommand.CanExecute(object?)&quot;/&gt; methods.&lt;/summary&gt;
        /// &lt;param name=&quot;execute&quot;&gt;Method for &lt;see cref=&quot;ICommand.Execute(object?)&quot;/&gt;.&lt;/param&gt;
        /// &lt;param name=&quot;canExecute&quot;&gt;Method for &lt;see cref=&quot;ICommand.CanExecute(object?)&quot;/&gt;.&lt;/param&gt;
        /// &lt;returns&gt;&lt;see cref=&quot;RelayCommand&quot;/&gt;.&lt;/returns&gt;
        /// &lt;exception cref=&quot;ArgumentNullException&quot;&gt;&lt;paramref name=&quot;execute&quot;/&gt; or
        /// &lt;paramref name=&quot;canExecute&quot;/&gt; is &lt;see langword=&quot;null&quot;/&gt;.&lt;/exception&gt;
        public static RelayCommand Create(Action&lt;object?&gt; execute, Predicate&lt;object?&gt; canExecute)
            =&gt; new RelayCommandExecute(execute, canExecute);
    }
</code></pre>
<p>Using:</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>    var comm1 = RelayCommand.Create(SomeExecuteMethod);
    var comm2 = RelayCommand.Create(SomeExecuteMethod, SomeCanExecuteMethod);
</code></pre>
<p>Or:</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>using static SomeNameSpace.RelayCommand;


            var comm1 = Create(SomeExecuteMethod);
            var comm2 = Create(SomeExecuteMethod, SomeCanExecuteMethod);
</code></pre>
